.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "BSDSF24A012-OS-A01" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- find lines containing a search string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mygrep
reads lines from
.I fp
and finds lines containing
.IR search_str .
It allocates an array of copied matching lines and stores its address in
.IR matches .
The caller is responsible for freeing every returned line and then the array.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines, or -1 if an argument is NULL, allocation
fails, or a read error occurs.
